linux-6.12-rockchip (6.12.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian: switch to fragment-based kconfig.
    In order to reduce maintenance effort and ensure most config options are
    kept in sync across our various kernel packages, using fragment-based
    configuration allows using a single, very small device-specific fragment
    along with shared generic configuration.
    This doesn't produce an identical defconfig, although the changes
    shouldn't affect device support (although they would likely increase
    build duration).
  * Rebase on 6.12.2

 -- Arnaud Ferraris <aferraris@debian.org>  Thu, 05 Dec 2024 16:05:16 +0100

